Rule 1 (inputs must not be complex tensors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_2) ≠ 10
>>
Rule 2 (inputs must be broadcast-compatible with equal ranks)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 3 (out, if provided, must be a tensor)
{v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (out shape must match the broadcasted shape of input and other)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_3) = ndim(v_1) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ((shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)) ∨ (shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_2, i)) ∨ (shape(v_2, i) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, i) = shape(v_1, i)))
>>
Rule 5 (out must not be complex and should match one input dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_3) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_3) ≠ 10 ∧ (dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_1) ∨ dtype_(v_3) = dtype_(v_2))
